This page continues the definition of a 'figure' begun on p.1 of 'Analysis situs (première mouture)', GF IV, dated 10 June 1986. The aim is a set-theoretic and topological model of the combinatorics of a 'modèle de forme' (shape model), in the case of a 'construit'.

Setting. E is a Hausdorff space, or a tame ('modéré') space for a given tame theory. In the tame case, 'closed' means 'tame closed'.

Definition of a figure. A figure F of E is a closed subset X (its support |F|) together with a family of nonempty closed subsets X_i ('closed strata') with X = ∪X_i. The strata are ordered by inclusion: i ≤ j iff X_i ⊂ X_j. The conditions are:
(a) each X_i is closed;
(b) the family is locally finite;
(c) if X_i ⊊ X_j, then X_i is rare (nowhere dense) in X_j;
(d) put Ẋ_i = ∂X_i = ∪_{j<i} X_j. By (a)-(c) this set is closed in X_i, so int(X_i) := X_i \ ∂X_i is open in X_i. It is nonempty, because X_i ≠ ∅ and a locally finite union of closed nowhere-dense subsets is nowhere dense. It is required to be (1) a manifold (a tame manifold in the tame case) and (2) connected;
(e) a marginal, partly illegible frontier-type condition relating X_i, X_j, ∂X_j and the open stratum X_i°;
(f) X_i ∩ X_j is a union of strata X_k.

Equivalent description. A figure is just its set of strata, a subset F ⊂ P_f(X) (X is recovered as ∪X_i) satisfying (a)-(f). One then fixes a set 𝓕 of 'admissible' figures, 𝓕 ⊂ P(P_f(E)).

The projection Σ → 𝓕. To each F one attaches the poset Σ_F of its strata. One forms the total set Σ = ⨿_{F∈𝓕} Σ_F, projecting to 𝓕. Its points are the pairs (F, X_i) with X_i ∈ F. The NB notes that in the case at hand Σ_F ≅ F canonically.

What comes next (p.3). Sub-figures F' ⊂ F correspond to down-closed subsets of Σ_F. 'Elementary' figures are those whose Σ_F has a largest element. So Σ → 𝓕 is the beginning of a Grothendieck-construction-type object: a poset (or category) of strata fibred over the poset of figures. The resulting combinatorial datum (𝓕, Σ, orders) is meant to be the 'combinatorics of a shape'.

In modern terms: a closed, locally finite stratification by a poset, with connected manifold open strata and a frontier-type condition. This is a CS/poset-stratified-space notion close to regular cell or stratified complexes. It sits inside a chosen family of such stratifications, ordered by 'sub-figure'.
